sorder or that she is  necessarily restricting or that she's  throwing up her food none of that is  necessarily truth we don't know that I  don't know that I am admittedly just a  little bit troubled by what to say here  because the reality is I don't know  everything about Stephanie all I see is  the videos that she posts but from what  I do see I do potentially have some  concerns her experience here does remind  me a little bit of Stephanie  better mores extreme hunger as she went  through her all-in journey but from what  we saw with Stephanie's better mores  experience that extreme hunger was a  result of extreme caloric restriction  which totally altered her hunger and  satiety hormones and actually damaged a  number of biological functions it's  actually true that in these  circumstances that is when you have a  history of restriction and associated  low body fat percentage the body may  actually need a drastic amount of  calories to provide basic nutrition for  you know daily needs  plus extra to repair the damage what can  happen is that your enteric nervous  system which is the reflex circuits in  your gut is receiving information that  you're physically full yet the central  nervous system aka your brain is  receiving information that more energy  is required to return to a balanced  state so in this case the drive to eat a  lot of calories even like 10,000  calories which we see in some of these  eating challenge days is very normal in  this circumstance and it should be  honored as it's all about energy  restoration or building back what is  maybe not working optimally there is  good evidence to support this process as  crazy as it may sound to a lot of people  so I will link to some really good  resources below now I want to reiterate  that we don't know if this Stephanie is  restricting on the days that she maybe  isn't showing on her channel like we  know that Stephanie but are more of us  restricting but I just want to share the  information on what we do know about  extreme hunger in general again I'm not  suggesting that this is Stephanie's  experience what I can say is that  between these three 180-day videos never  mind the official eating challenges that  she puts up there is a huge range in  caloric consumption according to our  calculations  Stephanie consumed around 3,000 calories  on day one  1,750 calories on day two and a total of  11,000 430 calories on day 3  that is quite the range and after  looking at her macros her fat intake is  either on the higher end of the 20 to  35% total caloric recommendation or  totally surpasses it now again it is  normal very very normal for us not to  eat the same amount of calories every  day but these discrepancies are pretty  extreme once that he suggested that the  average daily caloric variability for  women should be usually between plus or  minus 25% other total energy needs which  would mean that Stephanie's caloric  intake just based on these three days  would probably sit somewhere between  1650 and 2,750 calories but from these  three videos only one of Stephanies what  Aeneid days actually falls within this  range and I assume if we were to also  factor in a lot of her other eating  challenge videos we would see even a  greater discrepancy also even if  Stephanie is in the bulk phase which I'm  just speculating by her use of hashtags  like hashtag gains on her Instagram her  day 3 contains substantially more food  than what we would probably typically  see and even a man's bulk phase again  everyone's normal needs are super unique  but I'm just speaking to a verges and  patterns that I see I would also say  that even if this variability is normal  for her and is not the result of extreme  hunger or previous restriction which  they very well may be again I cannot  deny her that legitimate possibility I  would have really liked to see her meet  those needs in a more balanced way this  is my major take home sugar salt and  saturated fat are all fine in moderation  but there are days when she's getting  ten times the amount of sodium sixteen  times the amount of saturated fat and  six times the amount of sugar the body  needs like we mentioned excessive intake  of sodium is linked with bloating and  high blood pressure which can put one at  risk for heart disease too much sugar  can also increase the risk of heart  disease as well as other chronic  diseases especially if she's going to  continue with these eating challenges  or even more extreme I would just want  her to be mindful of her everyday usual  normal diet now are there any  problematic claims or assumptions made  by this channel so I actually really  really like Stephanie's attitude towards  food we don't see Stephanie using any  deity language whatsoever in her videos  she also does not seem to be overly  preoccupied with her weight or how much  she eats or what she eats or how many  calories are in what she eats which I  really like I would just flag that again  some of the content in her channel here  may be triggering for a lot of people  who are struggling with their  relationship with food because her  behaviors can read as problematic even  if they are not actually problematic for  her if that makes sense  finally what can we take away from  Stephanie's channel I would say the  biggest takeaway for me is Stephanie's  glowing and fun personality I love that  she loves food and for me she herself is  really a pleasure to watch even if I  sometimes feel a little uncomfortable  watching her kind of eating challenge  days  bottom line though I do appreciate  Stephanie's enthusiasm and openness with  food I do worry about how this may be  interpreted by her viewers who may have  struggled or are currently struggling  with disordered eating or an eating  disorder it is totally healthy and  balanced to enjoy pizza or a matcha  flavored donut from time to time it is  also ok to occasionally eat a lot of  peanut butter off of a spoon but taken  together with t